  "note": " Samples alignment (docs/design/samples-definition.md): the packets of a page that fails its CRC and the packets with bytes present of a truncated page, and a packet left unfinished at the end of the stream, are handed to the codec parser, the cut ones flagged; a stream gains lostSamples and the statistics node Lost Samples. bad-crc, truncated-page, huge-lacing and eos-inside-packet gain packets (their packet and statistics nodes change), frames-corrupt counts a packet with missing frames by the frames present.",
